WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
- [Narrator] Over the past few years,

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.510
one Chinese company has thrived

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.580
in the online fast fashion industry

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.240
reaching a valuation of 66
billion dollars in 2023,

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.000
and controlling 40% of the U.S. market.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.110
It's-

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:13.943
- Shein.
- Shein.

00:00:13.943 --> 00:00:14.776
- I say Shein.

00:00:14.776 --> 00:00:16.777
- It's Shein.
- Shein is known for

00:00:16.777 --> 00:00:19.170
$2 T-shirts and $7 pants

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.693
with prices even lower
than its competitors.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.520
Shein made its U.S debut in 2015,

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.200
and the brand's sales exploded

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.470
during the pandemic growing
sixfold in two years.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.270
The company generated an estimated

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.330
23 billion dollars in revenue in 2022.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.730
And its filed to go public in the U.S.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.700
- Shein takes fast fashion
to a different level,

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.850
and they're on top of every micro trend.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.140
- [Narrator] But there's a larger story

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.823
behind Shein's low prices.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.000
A congressional report
found that Shein uses

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.950
a tax exemption to cut costs,

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.510
and the company released a report

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:57.870
that cited cases of involuntary
labor in its supply chain.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.093
This is the economics of Shein.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.890
Scrolling through Shein's
website can feel endless.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:07.440
- We offer thousands of new items per day.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.758
- [Narrator] But Shein
only initially produces

00:01:09.758 --> 00:01:12.330
100 to 200 units of each new product.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.060
- Shein's designs originate
with Shein designers

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.520
and with our Shein X
third-party designers.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.470
- [Narrator] As customers
browse those designs,

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.730
Shein has technology

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.250
that monitors user engagement activity.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.110
When a customer shows interest in an item

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.000
by hovering over it, clicking on it,

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.820
or adding it to their
cart, Shein takes note,

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.500
then it creates new designs

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.510
based on data from popular items.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.190
This way, the retailer can test

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.770
how popular an item is with its customers.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.560
If it does well, Shein
starts producing more.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.540
- This differs from traditional retail

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.763
where orders can often
be placed in the 10,000

00:01:45.763 --> 00:01:47.940
to 100,000 copies of a garment

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.240
and can be placed between three
and six months in advance.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.610
- [Narrator] And while it's
fast at creating new designs,

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.650
it's also quick to go through them.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.270
A Boston Consulting group report

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:00.900
found that Shein has an inventory
turnover rate of 40 days.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.820
That same report found that Shein

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:03.840
is twice as fast

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:07.020
as other competitor
retailers like H&amp;M and Zara.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.980
- The small batch model is a
matter of controlling the cost

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.260
and controlling the inventory wastage

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.900
so that they won't have
a large number of clothes

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.080
that are sitting unsold in
their warehouses in China

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.540
or in the U.S. or anywhere
else in the world.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.330
- [Narrator] The company
calls this an on-demand model,

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.250
and to support this on-demand model

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.900
and lower prices,

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.750
Shein hires thousands of
smaller manufacturers.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.010
It took the journal to film

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.190
in one of its third-party
supplier factories in Dongguan.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:39.780
- Our designers will
identify an item, design it,

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.220
prepare a spec for it,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.130
and then they'll put it into
our supplier management system,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.100
which will identify a
contract manufacturer.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.100
That contract manufacturer
will procure the supplies

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.260
necessary to produce that garment

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.410
from a network of suppliers
that Sheen has approved.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.210
- [Narrator] If a design is popular,

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.080
Shein's ordering platform

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.060
can automatically place another order

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.670
with its platform working in real time.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:06.060
- They're able to see as
demand for a particular product

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:09.210
is either waxing or
waning in the marketplace

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.610
so they can adjust their
operations accordingly.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.100
And this concentration of information

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.330
allows our suppliers

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.240
to efficiently structure
their own business

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.940
to be able to meet
demand at near real time.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.980
- [Narrator] By ordering
in smaller batches.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.090
Shein says it can reduce

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.460
the risk of excess unsold inventory.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:29.250
- It means that we don't
carry excess inventory waste

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.570
when we produce garments.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:34.650
That saves around 30 to
40% in cost of goods sold

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:35.910
on the garments alone.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.160
- [Narrator] But while less
inventory waste in the factory

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.020
may lower prices for consumers,

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.550
environmental activists say

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.400
it might not lead to lower
waste levels overall.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.050
- [Shen Lu] Critics are saying that

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:49.140
because Shein's clothing is so cheap,

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.970
people are buying a lot of it.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.850
And because fashion conscious young people

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.940
may retire some of their Shein quicker

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.790
than other more expensive clothing

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:03.090
that actually may cost inventory wastage

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.520
after the consumption happened.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.713
- Oh my goodness, there's so much.

00:04:09.977 --> 00:04:12.390
- [Narrator] A 2023 UBS report

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.610
found that the average U.S. Shein shopper

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.940
reported spending $100 per
month on women's clothing.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.600
That's about 60% more than the
average U.S. female consumer

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.970
and critics argue that
there's even more behind

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:26.580
how the brand is able to keep prices low.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.130
- Retailer Shein is in
hot water once again.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.590
- Shein has faced
accusations of worker abuse.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.450
- The brand has recently come under fire.

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.490
- Shein's on demand business model

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.940
is not the only reason why
its products are so cheap.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.660
It's also benefiting from
cheap labor in China.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.610
- Shein has not been fully transparent

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:45.843
about its supply chains.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.260
In 2022, Shein released the results

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.730
of its supplier audits,

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.470
but unlike some other retailers,

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:53.820
Shein didn't disclose

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:56.490
who its suppliers were or
where they were located.

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.320
The audits reported some incidents

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:01.320
that involve what the company
calls involuntary labor,

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.390
but didn't mention exactly how many

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:05.250
or where these incidents occurred.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.960
The Wall Street Journal's calculations

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:10.200
found that these audits
accounted for about 36%

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.540
of Shein's contracted manufacturers.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.767
The company said in a statement
to the Wall Street Journal,

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:16.530
"Shein is committed to providing

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.330
a safe and fair work environment

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.220
for all our suppliers employees.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.950
We pay manufacturing
suppliers competitive rates

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:25.620
so they can pay fair
wages to their workers."

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.440
Shein says it's committed
about $70 million

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.570
towards improving supplier
factory conditions

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:31.800
and training workers.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.500
Congress is investigating
Shein's labor practices

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.480
and whether the company sources cotton

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.460
from China's Xinjiang region.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:41.130
The U.S. government has
accused Chinese authorities

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:44.610
of using forced Muslim Uyghur
labor, which Beijing denies.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.100
- Some U.S. lawmakers have pushed Shein

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.860
to be more transparent
about their supply chain.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:51.450
- [Narrator] In a statement to WSJ,

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.990
the company says it has zero
tolerance for forced labor,

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:57.690
does not have contract
manufacturers in Xinjiang

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.730
and doesn't source cotton from China.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.530
Fashion Analysts say

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:02.910
Shein hasn't provided evidence

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.230
to back up these statements

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.000
including a list of its suppliers,

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.130
which goes against industry standard.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.020
And in addition to its on-demand model

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.280
and low labor costs,

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.140
Shein also keeps prices low

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.750
by taking advantage of
a U.S. tax exemption,

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.430
which allows low-valued packages

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.380
to enter the U.S. tariff-free.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:21.030
Under the de minimis tax rule,

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.700
shipments sent to individual
buyers in the U.S.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:27.900
aren't subject to tariffs if
they're worth less than $800.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:28.980
According to a report

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:30.810
from the U.S. House of Representatives,

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:34.470
30% of all packages shipped
to the United States each day

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:37.950
under the de minimis rule are
from Shein and its rival Temu.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.240
Between the two companies,

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:41.640
that adds up to millions of packages.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.770
Shein says that it supports reforming

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.930
the de minimis exemption.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:48.630
Meanwhile, the valuation has fallen.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:52.230
The company's $100
billion valuation in 2022

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:55.620
dropped by a third in a fundraising
round earlier this year,

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:58.020
and Temu, which launched last September,

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.560
overtook a larger share of
the U.S. market last June.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.260
Recently, Shein has tried
to improve its image

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.280
through social media

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.040
amidst environmental and labor criticisms,

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.570
but with limited success.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.370
Shein brought a group of influencers

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:12.780
to tour factories in China.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.000
- [Shen Lu] The tour
didn't really help address

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.960
a lot of the criticisms that
people have about Shein.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.970
- [Narrator] The company has
also moved its headquarters

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.980
from Nanjing China to Singapore.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.710
Shein is also trying to
diversify its supply chain

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.910
outside of China.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:27.930
With this move,

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:31.500
Shein is also adding new
manufacturers in other countries.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.480
Although the majority
of Shein's supply chain

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.710
is still in China,

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.980
the company promised
to invest $150 million

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.380
to train 2000 Brazilian manufacturers

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:42.000
over the next three years.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:45.060
And Shein has recently
partnered with Forever 21

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.740
and acquired roughly one third

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:49.500
of the fashion brand's
operator, Spark Group.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.060
- Shein has in recent months,

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:53.580
been trying to pivot
to a marketplace model,

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:56.160
which allows third-party sellers

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:59.190
to sell products directly to consumers

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:01.350
as Shein expands globally

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:04.710
and is trying to capture more
of market share in the U.S.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.753
and in other countries around the world.

00:08:07.742 --> 00:08:10.325
(upbeat music)

